<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<policyDefinitionResources xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" revision="1.0" schemaVersion="1.0" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/GroupPolicy/2006/07/PolicyDefinitions">
  <displayName>Foghorn desktop alerts</displayName>
  <description>Settings for the Foghorn desktop alert client. Foghorn was designed and built by Archie Paice (hello@archiepaice.com).</description>
  <resources>
    <stringTable>
      <string id="SUPPORTED_Foghorn">Windows 10, Windows 11 and Windows Server 2016 or later, with the Foghorn client installed</string>
      <string id="Cat_Foghorn">Foghorn</string>
      <string id="Cat_Foghorn_Help">Settings for the Foghorn desktop alert client.

Foghorn was designed and built by Archie Paice (hello@archiepaice.com).</string>
      <string id="ServerConnection">Foghorn server connection</string>
      <string id="ServerConnection_Help">Tells the Foghorn client on each computer where your Foghorn server is.

Server address: the full address of the server including the port, for example http://foghorn01:8080 or https://foghorn.college.local

Client key: copy this from the Foghorn web console, under Settings, Client key.

Settings made here take priority over anything the installer saved on the computer. The client picks up a change within about a minute of Group Policy refreshing; nobody needs to log off.

If this policy is Not Configured or Disabled, the client uses the settings saved by Install-FoghornClient (if any).</string>
      <string id="UseSystemProxy">Connect through the system web proxy</string>
      <string id="UseSystemProxy_Help">By default the Foghorn client connects straight to the Foghorn server and ignores any web proxy, because the server is normally on your own network.

Enable this only if computers can reach the Foghorn server solely through the proxy configured in Windows.</string>
    </stringTable>
    <presentationTable>
      <presentation id="ServerConnection">
        <textBox refId="ServerUrl">
          <label>Server address (e.g. http://foghorn01:8080)</label>
        </textBox>
        <textBox refId="ClientKey">
          <label>Client key</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
    </presentationTable>
  </resources>
</policyDefinitionResources>
